{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Troubles at Home"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Crossed Wires"}, {"type": "position", "content": 3}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe ways of solving problems and getting things done in social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn9le01ob03re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Need to be Fixed or Needs Fixing"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Need +passive infinitive</span> and <span class=\"strong\">need+verb+ing</span> are two structures you use to talk about fixing problems. You use these structures to imply that we don't know who will fix the problem, or that the person fixing the problem is not the focus of the sentence."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Subject + <span class=\"italic\">Need</span> + Passive Infinitive"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">There is so much that needs to be fixed around here!</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "The subject of the sentence is the thing that needs fixing/to be fixed."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Subject + <span class=\"italic\">Need</span> + Verb + <span class=\"italic\">ing</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">I have realized that a couple of lamps need repairing.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<br/><span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">Need</span> + Verb + <span class=\"italic\">ing</span></span>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Subject\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Form of need\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"  Main Verb + <span class=\\\"italic\\\">ing</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" A couple of lamps\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"need\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" repairing.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"  ... that\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"needs\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" fixing.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"The entire building that\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" needs\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" rewiring.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": " I have realized that a couple of lamps <span class=\"strong\">need repairing</span>."}, {"type": "example", "content": " It <span class=\"strong\">needs to be repaired</span>. "}, {"type": "example", "content": " It's possible that it isn't the lamp that <span class=\"strong\">needs fixing</span>."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Maybe it's the entire building that <span class=\"strong\">needs rewiring</span>! "}, {"type": "example", "content": "There is so much that <span class=\"strong\">needs to be fixed</span> around here! "}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Language of Reaction"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "We use paralanguage to react to a situation. These are sounds you use to show an emotional reaction."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Here are some examples:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! - shows a mistake or error has been made."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Ow! - shows pain."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Shhh! - shows you want people to be quiet."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Dammit! - shows anger or frustration."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Whoops! "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Ow! Ow! Ouch that hurt."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Shhhh! I am trying to watch this podcast."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Well ... dammit! "}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to electrocute"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to get injured by an electric shock"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Well, don't electrocute yourself! "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le01ob03aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about household problems."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to unplug"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to disconnec